# UI translations (next-intl)

This app uses **next-intl** with locale files in `messages/` (`en`, `fr`, `de`, `es`). English is the source of truth; other locales merge over `en` at runtime (`src/i18n/request.ts`), but **every user-visible string must exist in all four JSON files** with proper translations — not English placeholders in `fr`/`de`/`es`.

## When adding or changing UI

1. **Never hard-code user-visible text** in components/pages. Use `useTranslations("namespace")` or `getTranslations` on the server.
2. **Add the key to `messages/en.json` first**.
3. **Add the same key path to `messages/fr.json`, `messages/de.json`, and `messages/es.json`**.
4. **Run `npm run i18n:check`** before finishing.
